Licence posture, recorded 2026-08-15
------------------------------------

This licence matches what the application actually links today. The
reconstruction depends only on AndroidX and Jetpack Compose (Apache-2.0), so
MIT is the strongest obligation in force and the app carries no copyleft.

Two planned dependencies would change that, and the change is mechanical rather
than a decision to revisit:

- BELABOX `srtla` is AGPL-3.0. Linking it for bonding makes the distributed
  application AGPL-3.0 as a whole, obliging an offer of source to anyone who
  receives a build. This repository is already public, so the practical cost is
  replacing this file and stating the obligation.
- Haivision `libsrt` is MPL-2.0, a file-level copyleft that arrives with any SRT
  implementation. It is satisfied by publishing modifications to MPL files and
  does not affect the licence of the application as a whole.

Neither is linked at the time of writing. See `replica-app/docs/known-deviations.md`
(D011) and `RESEARCH.md`.
